  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Increased institutional capacity of labour administrations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Effective labour market governance requires effective, accountable and inclusive labour administration systems, based on sound labour laws and social dialogue. Labour administrations will be supported through comprehensive and tailor-made assessments of the systems, capacity-building packages, including policy advice, advocacy and training as well as global knowledge products and tools to help them engage in efforts towards an enhanced ministries of labour -or similar institutions- for the effective governance of work. The following are the major global deliverables and activities of the ILO in this policy area.
(1) Knowledge and advocacy initiatives and products for stronger systems of labour administration and inspection, based on ILO Conventions and guidelines and the practical application and evaluation of the use of the UN Principles of Effective Governance for Sustainable Development.
(2) Advocacy and multilateral action to promote coherence of policy approaches of international financial institutions with ILO standards and address the views of the ILO&#x2019;s supervisory bodies
(3) Policy and capacity-building tools to upscale the role of labour administration, including labour inspection, in the work of UN country teams
(4) Support to regional networks, platforms, events and peer-to-peer exchanges on labour administration and inspection, including through an academy and trainings organized with the Turin Centre.</narrative>
  </description>
